diff --git a/docs/docker-deployment.md b/docs/docker-deployment.md
index f6eca78..e0439e3 100644
--- a/docs/docker-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/docker-deployment.md
@@ -101,6 +101,25 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Web push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send notifications to people's phones and desktops, so they hear about things as they land in their tray.
+People turn it on for each device from their notification settings.
+
+To enable it, generate a VAPID key pair and set both halves of it:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}", "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+```sh
+docker run --env VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=... --env VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=... ...
+```
+
+Keep the private key secret.
+If you change the key pair later, people will need to turn notifications on again on each of their devices.
+Notification links are built from `BASE_URL`, so set that too.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
